field.value:
For a positive measurement rounded using the usual rule that a halfway value rounds up, the **limits of accuracy** are $\text{lower bound} \leq \text{true value} < \text{upper bound}$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\fill[blue!20] (2,-0.15) rectangle (9,0.15);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,0) -- (11.6,0);
\draw (2,-0.25) -- (2,0.25);
\draw (5.5,-0.25) -- (5.5,0.25);
\draw (9,-0.25) -- (9,0.25);
\node[below] at (2,-0.3) {$m-e$};
\node[below] at (5.5,-0.3) {$m$};
\node[below] at (9,-0.3) {$m+e$};
\node[above] at (2,0.3) {lower bound};
\node[above] at (5.5,0.3) {measurement};
\node[above] at (9,0.3) {upper bound};
\node[above] at (5.5,1.3) {true value lies in the shaded band};
\end{tikzpicture}
